stars are a pervasive form of power in  the lands between they comprise a big  part of ronnie's ending they connect  sorcerers to magical power they are  likely where most outer gods reside and  they are the source of quite a few of  the game's bosses we saw one star sent  alien in my discussion of the elden  beast and today i want to look at its  connection to another creature of the  stars the equally mysterious estelle  natural born of the void  we previously learned that the elden  beast is a being sent to the lands  between by the greater will it came on a  golden star it was set up as a defense  for the elden ring to ensure that it  operated according to the greater will's  desires with that foundation we can turn  our attention to estelle to  cross-reference for any connection and  as we delve into this new lore feel free  to subscribe to the channel to keep up  to date with all of my lore and elden  ring content  as for any notable boss a great starting  point to look at is its remembrance the  remembrance of the natural born tells us  that estelle is a malformed star born in  the flightless void far away once  destroyed an eternal city and took away  their sky a falling star of ill omen  more than a whole video could be  dedicated to deciphering this and the  rest of estelle's story so for the  purposes of this video i will be taking  the lead from v limits insightful  account i highly recommend you check out  his video on estelle so because estelle  destroyed an eternal city it could be  assumed that they were on the side of  the greater will and eldon beast perhaps  just another star sent to enforce the  greater will's plans after all the knox  which inhabit the eternal cities had in  the past invoked the ire of the greater  will and were banished deep underground  with the inhabitants of the eternal  cities being enemies of the greater will  enemies who went so far as to fashion  the finger slayer blade to kill its  vassal two fingers it is easy to think  that estelle would be on the greater  wills side by being seen as an enemy of  the nox but v-limit illustrates that  this might not be the case  if we look at the description of  estelle's remembrance closely we will  see that the two named eternal cities  nocron and noxtella don't quite fit the  description of having been destroyed and  robbed of their sky  both of the cities have many  non-destroyed architecture as well as  star-filled skies the skies are noted to  be false but they're still there in  contrast there is one more eternal city  which is more properly destroyed and  devoid of sky in the deep root depths  there is a grace that reveals the area  to be that of a forgotten nameless  eternal city now we only have reference  of the greater will banishing the nox  not destroying them or their cities this  led v-limit to posit that estelle might  have been created or harnessed by the  nox as a means of attack against the  greater will only to have their creature  turn against them level their city and  steal their sky  this would track with the fact that  despite there being two estelle the  natural born of the void at the end of  ronnie's quest and the stars of darkness  in the consecrated snowfield only one of  them has a night sky in their boss fight  arena the natural born has a star-filled  night sky just like those of the eternal  cities whereas the stars of darkness  introduces no unique atmosphere or sky  if only one sky were stolen as it seems  to be the case since only one eternal  city is missing a sky then we would only  expect to see one sky bearing estelle if  the greater will had sicked estelle onto  the nox and eternal cities i would think  that multiple estelle would mean  multiple cities destroyed and multiple  skies taken but that doesn't happen  if instead the estelle were some product  of a noxian plan then the single city  destruction could make sense if the knox  were only attempting that plan in one  city we know from their other creations  such as the mimic tears and the finger  slayer blade that the knocks were open  to trying anything and everything in  their aims of fighting back against the  greater will so making a few estelle  could seem plausible  so maybe the estelle are not an arm of  the greater will and instead a creation  of the knox if this is the case how did  the knox bring them about the greater  will could have just sent them in from  space like it does the elden beast at  least that's all the description we get  the nox not being outer gods likely  would have needed some specific method  to do this we might be able to learn of  these means by looking at what seems to  be another form of estelle that is the  falling star beasts the falling star  beasts are found in meteor impacts  throughout the lands between because of  their similar pincers gravity magic a  similar-looking growth in the case of  the full-grown falling star beast and  the fact that the natural-born's  remembrance explicitly calls estelle a  falling star the connections between  these two kinds of beings are undeniable  estelle are some derivative offshoot  evolution or some other form of the  falling star beasts b limit thinks that  the nox formed estelle out of the  falling star beasts giving them their  human-like influence the arms and skull  and i think this or something like it is  plausible  looking at the more prominent of the two  estelle's epithet a natural born or a  natural child is a euphemism for an  illegitimate child or a bastard the  remembrance can also be formed into a  weapon called the bastard's stars which  reads  formed of the same many-colored star  debris that comprise the form of the  natural born of the void  these themes speak to the fact that  estelle's birth or creation was in some  way unnatural or improper estelle was  born in the wrong way though in what  manner this birth is wrong is hard to  say for certain a right birth is likely  what the falling star beasts count as so  the most plausible explanation to me  would be that the knock somehow  interfered with some of the falling star  beasts likely when they were still stars  in space or first coming upon the lands  between  somehow the nox influenced or corrupted  the falling stars they had influence  over and turned them into what became a  stell  as v-limit points out if the nox wanted  something to contend with the greater  will and its star of the elden beast  what better than another star  and if we look at the two fights we come  to see a few threads of connection  despite their apparent dissimilarities  both of the fights take place in large  circular arenas both of the bosses have  some flavor of snake or serpentine  bodies and motion while many of their  attacks are different they both have a  painful grab and a star-like nebula  attack where they emit a cluster of  stars which then explode on a delay the  clusters do appear a bit different in  line with the different themes of each  boss estelle's is more purple and silver  the elden beast's is more red and gold  the silver of the nox against the gold  of the order  again taking an idea from v limit  seriously go watch his video  the experience one goes through in each  fight also share similarities as the  bosses bear a similar overall size and  rough shape attacking each one ends up  following like strategies the heads are  focal points to target but often end up  moving around enough to justify going  for appendages or body shots dodging  grabs and front-facing arm attacks is  contrasted with avoiding projectiles  raining down from the heavens in both  bites one could maybe say that the  similar fight experience and strategy is  due to the bosses being a similar type  and size and leave it alone there kind  of as a artifact of from soft just  making similar kinds of big bosses but  with the lore that fromsoft has written  in the game that connects these two a  deeper connection and rationale for the  similar fights is pretty hard to argue  with on a story perspective  as rival sources of star power estelle  and the elden beast seem well matched  something like two sides of a coin  though we do see more than one estelle  and there is a potential for even more  since there are so many falling star  beasts whereas the elden beast seems  more one of a kind  and as the singular envoy of the greater  will in addition to being the final boss  it does give it a bit more grandeur and  sense of power and scale  maybe the greater will has many more  beasts at its disposal like the many  seeming urgeries we see in the final  fights arena but in game we only see and  have evidence for the one if we really  want to speculate though the uniqueness  of estelle might be able to be defended  in some way if we take a step back and  remember that eldon ring is a game  filled to the brim with repurposed enemy  and boss assets for example there is  technically a lore justification for  them being different but in practicality  there are two godrics in the game one  got renamed to goad for and was given  just the teensy bit of story in the lore  to say they're different but in my  opinion the lore here seems very  derivative or after the fact of the  reusing of a story boss in an ever jail  it very well could have been the case  that estelle was a one of the kind who  then got the same treatment with a  sentence or two changed in the lore to  demarcate the natural born from the  stars of darkness and justify the reused  gameplay asset  we might be able to find justification  for this scene as estelle was one of the  most unique experiences in the game at  the culmination of ronnie's questline  only to lose its one-of-a-kind status to  a random boss repeat at the end of an  ice tunnel in a secondary optional area  in the game  though to not delve too far into a  critique of the game like the last video  we can't go further here without any  actual evidence from the game itself  which is something i don't think we have  the elden beast and estelle offer a  small kind of foil to one another  especially if they are in fact beasts of  opposing sides the greater will and the  knox unfortunately we don't have more  specific evidence to mull over to make  any further clear conclusions again in  like manner estelle is shrouded in  questions just as we saw with the elden  beast in a more dedicated exploration of  estelle and the stars the creatures from  the stars we might find a few more  answers about the nature of star  creatures and that could be a future  video on the channel but for now we have  seen the connection to the elden beast  despite a wealth of differences there  are a few threads that tie together  these otherworldly creatures if you  would like to join me in continuing this  journey through the lore and themes of  elden ring feel free to subscribe to the  channel or sign up to support me on  patreon where you get early access to  video scripts along with other perks in  addition to supporting the channel i  hope you've enjoyed watching and i'll  see you in the next video thanks bye
 

